  "question": {
    "text": "If the angle between the line $x=\\frac{y-1}{2}=\\frac{z-3}{\\lambda}$ and the plane $x+2 y+3 z=4$ is $\\cos ^{-1}\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{14}}\\right)$, then $\\lambda$ equals"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{3}{2}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{2}{5}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{5}{3}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{2}{3}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\cos \\theta=\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{14}}$\n$\\sin \\theta=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{14}}$\n$\\sin \\theta=\\frac{1+4+3 \\lambda}{\\sqrt{1+4+\\lambda^2} \\sqrt{1+4+9}}$\n$\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{14}}=\\frac{5+3 \\lambda}{\\sqrt{5+\\lambda^2} \\sqrt{14}} \\Rightarrow \\lambda=\\frac{2}{3}$"
  }
